Hosted Ezero behavioral acceptance

Build the tools with bash ezero/build.sh, then run:
  bash ezero/tests/run.sh
Use --list to list cases, --filter REGEX for an isolated subset, and
--output /absolute/new/empty/directory to choose the evidence location.

All parsing, typing, arithmetic, execution and memory reclamation under test
are implemented in original Zero code. Python and shell only write test inputs,
invoke the own toolchain and compare independent expected stdout/error results.
The suite never implements an Ezero evaluator or borrows a foreign runtime.
No network access, download, third-party package installation or VM is needed.

Coverage includes unquoted UTF-8 text and typed phrases, one-based indexing,
Unicode scalar count, optional quoted escape compatibility, automatic values,
checked unsigned arithmetic, lists, conditions, loops evaluated once, recursive
functions, call evaluation order, copied-frame isolation, garbage collection,
clear runtime failures, compile source locations and output preservation.
Boundary cases exercise source/string/variable/parameter/instruction limits.

The generated executables run on the existing Linux host. This is not a claim
that Ezero programs run inside Zero OS, whose application loader is separate
work. Test artifacts are private build output, not a new distributed disk image.
Reports record exact implementation hashes. Passing results must be read from
the completed report; this source file itself makes no pass claim.
